  <prompt>Implement H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler in `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core\Handlers\KvSecretsPopulation\` alongside the existing H4 handler (task 047). H4-shared is the SIBLING of H4: same `KvSecretsPopulationOptions`, same `IKvSecretsWriter` (SDK-based `SecretClientKvWriter`), same `IArmKeyVaultRefProbe`, same `IKvSecretManifest` reader — but seeds the SHARED-tier KV by EXTRACTING credentials from source Azure services via Azure.ResourceManager SDK (AI Search admin key, Cognitive Services key1, Service Bus root SAS, Storage connection string, Redis composed connection string). Additively extends task 084's canonical secret-catalog manifest with a new `value_source: "from-shared-service"` enum value + conditional scalar `service_ref:` field on shared-tier entries. Idempotent: verify existing secret matches current source; only rotate on drift (audit-logged). All source extractors use Azure.ResourceManager.* SDK (NOT `az` CLI shell-out) for testability and pattern-alignment with H4.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the L2 4-project scaffold (`Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.{Api,Worker,Core,Tests}`), the `IProvisioningHandler` contract (returns `HandlerResult`, NOT exceptions for domain failures), Azure.ResourceManager SDK (`ArmClient` extension methods for Search/CognitiveServices/ServiceBus/Storage/Redis), Azure Key Vault + RBAC (Secrets Officer for write; Secrets User for read), the 3-file DI dance (`HandlerIds.cs` + `HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs` + `.Worker\Program.cs`), and the H4 exemplar (H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs — the canonical reference). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Files exist and the following contract is satisfied: (a) `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core\Handlers\KvSecretsPopulation\H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs` implements `IProvisioningHandler`; (b) new seam `ISourceServiceKeyExtractor` at same folder with `SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor` impl using Azure.ResourceManager SDK; (c) `IKvSecretValueResolver` gains new strategy for `value_source: "from-shared-service"` OR (equivalently) H4-shared handler resolves values directly via `ISourceServiceKeyExtractor` and passes to `IKvSecretsWriter`; (d) canonical manifest schema at `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` extended with `from-shared-service` enum value + optional scalar `service_ref:` field (conditionally required when `value_source == from-shared-service`); (e) `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` extended: `$AllowedValueSources` gains new value, `Test-ManifestShape` enforces conditional-required rule for `service_ref`, `-Verify` still exits 0 on unchanged inputs; (f) initial 6-entry F19 manifest additions committed (AiSearch--AdminKey, DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey, AzureOpenAI-ApiKey, servicebus-connection-string, storage-connection-string, redis-connection-string all with `value_source: "from-shared-service"` + `service_ref:`); (g) new `HandlerIds.H4Shared` const + entry in `Dispatchable` list; (h) `HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs` gains keyed factory forwarder; (i) `.Worker\Program.cs` gains concrete DI registrations (Options bind, seam Singletons, handler Scoped); (j) `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests\Handlers\H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandlerTests.cs` with hand-rolled fakes (per H4 test file exemplar) covering: 6-source-type happy path, source-drift rotation, existing-and-matching NO-OP, source-service-unreachable Quarantine, BINDING guard (never-delete secrets are NOT in H4-shared's target set), idempotency, cleartext-secret leak scan, manifest v1 backwards compat (entries without `service_ref` skipped, not errored); (k) `HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests` still passes; (l) `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` all exit 0.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
Per lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md finding F19 + Automation Gaps roadmap item 12 in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md`: Bicep provisions the shared KV `sprk-{env}-kv` but leaves it EMPTY. All 6 BFF `@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)` references point to non-existent secrets. Even after F16 fixes (RBAC + kvRefIdentity), refs cannot resolve. BFF fails-fast at boot on the downstream config chain (F20/F20a).

Session 2 (2026-08-24) manually seeded 6 secrets to `sprk-prod-kv` by extracting from source services via ad-hoc az CLI. Recipe worked; this task codifies the recipe as an IProvisioningHandler using Azure.ResourceManager SDK (NOT az CLI shell-out — aligns with H4's `SecretClientKvWriter` pattern).

**The 6 F19 extraction recipes** (validated live SESSION 2; codify as SDK calls):
| Canonical name | SDK call |
|---|---|
| `AiSearch--AdminKey` | `armClient.GetSearchServiceResource(id).GetAdminKeys().Value.PrimaryKey` |
| `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` | `armClient.GetCognitiveServicesAccountResource(id).GetKeys().Value.Key1` |
| `AzureOpenAI-ApiKey` | `armClient.GetCognitiveServicesAccountResource(id).GetKeys().Value.Key1` |
| `servicebus-connection-string` | `armClient.GetServiceBusNamespaceResource(id).GetServiceBusNamespaceAuthorizationRules().Get("RootManageSharedAccessKey").GetKeys().Value.PrimaryConnectionString` |
| `storage-connection-string` | `armClient.GetStorageAccountResource(id).GetKeys().First(k => k.KeyName == "key1").Value` composed as `DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=X;AccountKey=Y;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net` |
| `redis-connection-string` | `armClient.GetRedisResource(id)` for host+port; `.GetKeys().Value.PrimaryKey`; compose as `{host}:{port},password={key},ssl=True,abortConnect=False` |

**L2 project layout confirmed via recon 2026-08-24**: handlers live in `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core\Handlers\<Family>\`. H4 is at `.Core\Handlers\KvSecretsPopulation\H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs`. Seam interfaces + impls co-located same folder. The `.Worker` project owns dispatch (`Dispatch\ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher.cs`) + concrete DI registration (`.Worker\Program.cs`). Keyed factory forwarder lives in `.Core\Handlers\HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs`. HandlerIds catalog + Dispatchable list in `.Core\Handlers\HandlerIds.cs`. Tests in `.Tests\Handlers\<HandlerName>Tests.cs` (flat folder) using xunit + FluentAssertions + hand-rolled fakes (per H4 exemplar).

**Canonical manifest extension (additive, safe)**: Recon 2026-08-24 confirmed tasks 085 + 086 only read `canonical_name` + `aliases` from manifest entries. Generator uses `ContainsKey` (not strict-schema) shape check — unknown fields silently ignored. Adding `from-shared-service` enum value + optional `service_ref:` field does NOT break 085/086. But: any new required field MUST be added to `$RequiredSecretFields` (line 131-134 of Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1) OR handled as CONDITIONALLY required. Approach: extend `$AllowedValueSources` (line ~135) with `from-shared-service`; extend `Test-ManifestShape` with a conditional check: `if ($secret.value_source -eq 'from-shared-service' -and -not $secret.ContainsKey('service_ref')) { throw "..." }`. Generator outputs unchanged for existing entries; new shared-service entries emit into `Seed-CustomerKeyVault.generated.ps1` a new branch that documents "handler-populated" (comment-only; the actual writes come from H4-shared handler at run time, NOT from the seeder script).

**CLUSTER FINDING (from SESSION 2 handoff)**: F17 + F19 + F20 share ONE root cause — Bicep provisions Model 1 Prod infra but does NOT seed BFF runtime state. H4-shared (this task) + H4b (task 201) + H9 (task 052) together close this gap. Sequencing: H4-shared → H4b → H9 → BFF starts with all config in place (kills F20 progressive fail-fast).
    </background>
