  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Single `IProvisioningHandler` implementation returning `Task&lt;HandlerResult&gt;`. Domain failures are `HandlerResult.Failure(FailureClass, RejectionCode, Diagnostic)` — do NOT throw exceptions for expected failure modes (missing per-env parameter, source-service 403, drift). Exception-throw only for programmer errors (null argument, invalid state).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register in L2 control-plane, NOT BFF. Handler class in `.Core`; concrete DI in `.Worker\Program.cs`; keyed forwarder in `.Core\Handlers\HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth ceremony 21 MUSTs. L2 UAMI must hold data-plane read on each source (BICEP HARDENING FOLLOW-ON per escalation trigger below): `Cognitive Services User` (openai + docintel), `Search Service Contributor` (search-admin-key), `Azure Service Bus Data Owner` (SB RootManageSharedAccessKey list), `Storage Account Contributor` (storage key1 list), `Redis Cache Contributor` (Redis list-keys). H4-shared uses `TokenCredential` (defaults to `DefaultAzureCredential` per env; MI in Azure, dev-cred locally) — SAME as H4.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Reuse background-job infrastructure; return `HandlerResult`; fire-and-forget from L2 dispatcher.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key: `kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer}` — secretsVer is manifest hash from canonical secret-catalog (source-scoped entries subset).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-recon-2026-08-24">Manifest schema extension is ADDITIVE (safe per recon confirming 085/086 only read `canonical_name` + `aliases`): add `from-shared-service` to `$AllowedValueSources` enum in `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1`; add optional scalar `service_ref:` field; `Test-ManifestShape` gets conditional required rule: if `value_source == from-shared-service` then `service_ref` MUST be present. NO change to `$RequiredSecretFields` (line 131-134) — `service_ref` is CONDITIONALLY required, not always required.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-recon-2026-08-24">Regenerated outputs MUST be committed atomically with manifest edits — `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify` MUST exit 0 after the task lands. This is the shipped determinism contract task 084 established.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Source-extraction uses Azure.ResourceManager SDK (NOT `az` CLI shell-out). Rationale: (a) aligns with H4's SecretClientKvWriter SDK pattern; (b) testable via seam mocking (hand-rolled fake `ISourceServiceKeyExtractor` per H4 test exemplar); (c) no process spawn overhead; (d) type-safe error handling (ARM SDK throws `RequestFailedException` with structured status codes — cleanly maps to HandlerResult.Failure).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-source-type extraction is declarative: `SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor` dispatches on `SourceServiceType` enum (parsed from manifest `service_ref` format like `search:sprksharedprod-search` or `cognitiveservices:sprksharedprod-openai`). NO ad-hoc bash. NO shelling out to per-secret one-off scripts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency: for each entry, compare current KV value against fresh source extraction; NO-OP if match (do NOT write same value twice — creates useless KV version bloat), rotate + audit-log if drift. Drift may indicate source-key rotation in Azure Portal (legitimate) OR unauthorized change (audit signal).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BINDING guard: NEVER write to Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret via this handler. Those two secrets have `never_delete: true` in manifest AND are NOT emitted as Bicep resources (comments only per task 084 design). H4-shared asserts these secret names never appear in shared-service-scoped manifest entries at handler startup validation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §7.9">Canonical KV secret naming applied at seed time: env-agnostic names; secret names MUST match the App Service `@Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretName=...)` references exactly (case-sensitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md NFR-05">BFF /health must fail fast at boot on any Tier-1 IOptions misconfig. H4-shared runs BEFORE H4b (task 201) + BEFORE H9 (task 052) so BFF boots with KV refs already resolvable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="F15+F18-remediation">Handler assumes L2 UAMI has already been granted `Key Vault Secrets Officer` on the shared KV via H4-preflight (task-TODO for operator-RBAC bootstrap; F15/F18 both fixed manually SESSION 2 — pre-check MUST run BEFORE H4-shared writes; if pre-check hasn't landed as a handler, escalate per §6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Post-condition: after all H4-shared writes, invoke `IArmKeyVaultRefProbe` (reused from H2a/H4) to verify each canonical name resolves via the App Service KV-ref binding. Failure → `HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "SharedSecretRefUnresolvable", diagnostic)` pointing to F16 / operator-RBAC gaps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§10">L2 handlers register in L2 DI, NOT in BFF (§10 BFF Hygiene). Publish-size verification applies to BFF only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§11">NEW-surface justification field completed per §11 three-question gate (see &lt;justification&gt; below).</constraint>
  </constraints>

