  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load knowledge files. Read H4 exemplar (task 047 handler + tests) end-to-end for ctor shape, HandlerResult semantics, idempotency-key format, BINDING guard code path.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Manifest schema extension">Extend `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1`: add `from-shared-service` to `$AllowedValueSources`; add conditional required rule to `Test-ManifestShape` (if `value_source == from-shared-service` then `service_ref` MUST be present). Add 6 F19 entries to `manifest.yaml` with `value_source: from-shared-service` + `service_ref: search:sprksharedprod-search` (etc. per env-scoped naming convention). Run `pwsh Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -DryRun`; inspect planned outputs.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Regenerate outputs">Run `pwsh Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` (write mode); confirm all 4 generated files updated. Run `-Verify` to confirm byte-identical regen.</step>
    <step order="3" name="ISourceServiceKeyExtractor seam">Author interface `ISourceServiceKeyExtractor.cs` in `.Core\Handlers\KvSecretsPopulation\`: `Task&lt;string&gt; ExtractAsync(SharedKvSecretSource source, CancellationToken ct)`. `SharedKvSecretSource` is a record: `{ SourceType (enum: AiSearchAdminKey|CognitiveServicesKey1|ServiceBusRootSas|StorageConnectionString|RedisComposed), ServiceRef, ResourceGroup?, SubscriptionId? }`. Errors surface as `RequestFailedException` propagation (handler wraps into HandlerResult.Failure).</step>
    <step order="4" name="SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor impl">Author `SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor.cs` — inject `ArmClient` (reused from H4 DI). Dispatch on `SourceType` enum: 6 branches, each ~10 lines. Each branch uses Azure.ResourceManager.* SDK per the table in &lt;context&gt;. Redis-composed branch composes the `{host}:{port},password={key},ssl=True,abortConnect=False` format string.</step>
    <step order="5" name="H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler impl">Author main handler mirroring H4 shape. Ctor injects: IProvisioningRunRepository, IKvSecretManifest, IKvSecretsWriter (reused), IArmKeyVaultRefProbe (reused), ISourceServiceKeyExtractor (new), IOptions&lt;KvSecretsPopulationOptions&gt; (reused OR new sibling if divergent config needed), ILogger. HandleAsync flow: (a) load manifest entries with `value_source == from-shared-service`; (b) BINDING guard: assert no entry name in never-delete list; (c) for each entry: ExtractAsync fresh source value → read current KV value → NO-OP on match, WriteAsync + audit on drift or absence; (d) invoke IArmKeyVaultRefProbe post-condition; (e) return `HandlerResult.Success(idempotencyKey)` or `HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, code, diagnostic)`; (f) idempotency key `kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer}`. HandlerId const: `HandlerIds.H4Shared`.</step>
    <step order="6" name="DI 3-file registration">(a) `.Core\Handlers\HandlerIds.cs`: add `public const string H4Shared = "h4-shared";` near H4 const line ~59; append to `Dispatchable` list (line ~122-125). (b) `.Core\Handlers\HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs`: add keyed forwarder `services.AddKeyedScoped&lt;IProvisioningHandler&gt;(HandlerIds.H4Shared, (sp,_) =&gt; sp.GetRequiredService&lt;H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler&gt;());` near line ~107. (c) `.Worker\Program.cs`: add concrete registrations near H4 block (lines ~394-478): `AddSingleton&lt;ISourceServiceKeyExtractor, SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor&gt;` + `AddScoped&lt;H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler&gt;()`.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Unit tests">Author `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandlerTests.cs` in `.Tests\Handlers\` (flat folder per H4 test exemplar). xunit + FluentAssertions + hand-rolled fakes. Tests: (a) 6-source-type happy path — mocked extractor returns known values for all 6 F19 entries; handler writes all 6 to KV; probe verifies; returns Success; (b) source-drift rotation — KV has "old", extractor returns "new" → WriteAsync called + audit log entry; (c) existing-and-matching NO-OP — KV value == extractor value → no WriteAsync call, no audit; (d) source-service-unreachable Quarantine — mocked extractor throws RequestFailedException(403) → HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "SourceServiceExtractionFailed", diagnostic naming service); (e) BINDING guard — synthetic manifest with Dataverse-ClientSecret as `value_source: from-shared-service` → handler validation fails at startup with "BindingPreCheckViolation"; (f) idempotency-key match — second run same (env, secretsVer) short-circuits via IIdempotencyService (mirror H4 pattern); (g) cleartext-secret leak scan — assert Cosmos parameters + all log statements contain 0 substrings from test-extractor return values; (h) manifest v1 backwards compat — entries without `value_source == from-shared-service` skipped by H4-shared (they belong to H4 per-tenant flow), no error.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Build + test">Run: `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/`. All exit 0. HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests must pass (new H4Shared const has keyed forwarder).</step>
    <step order="9" name="Regenerated-outputs Verify">Run `pwsh scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify`; exit 0 required. If drift: regenerate + commit.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Handler-catalog update (main-session)">Update handler catalog in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 3 enumeration: H4-shared row already listed there from SESSION 3; verify accuracy vs implemented handler (main-session-only per root CLAUDE.md §3 sub-agent write boundary).</step>
    <step order="11" name="TASK-INDEX update (main-session)">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 200 status 🔲 → ✅ with commit hash.</step>
    <step order="12" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-200-completion-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 084's `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` structure has drifted (e.g., `$AllowedValueSources` variable name renamed, `Test-ManifestShape` signature changed), STOP and diff against the SESSION 4 recon findings before editing.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any source Azure service returns 403 during H4-shared happy-path testing against Model 1 Prod (extractor gets Forbidden despite L2 UAMI existing), STOP and escalate — root cause is L2 UAMI missing one of the 5 RBAC assignments (`Cognitive Services User` / `Search Service Contributor` / `Azure Service Bus Data Owner` / `Storage Account Contributor` / `Redis Cache Contributor`). This is a Bicep hardening follow-on — file separate task for `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` (or `platform-shared.bicep`) to emit these role assignments for the L2 UAMI. Do NOT retry-loop; do NOT proceed to task 201.</trigger>
    <trigger>If `IArmKeyVaultRefProbe` verify-step fails after H4-shared writes (secret is on KV but App Service can't resolve the ref), STOP and escalate — F16 remediation gap OR kvRefIdentity misconfig OR shared UAMI RBAC not granted on shared KV. Do NOT proceed to H4b.</trigger>
    <trigger>If manifest schema extension breaks `-Verify` (regenerated outputs differ from on-disk after commit), STOP and diagnose: (a) generator emitter added output but forgot to re-verify; (b) new field emitted with different ordering; (c) determinism contract violated.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a new source-type is proposed later (not in the 6 F19 set) but no `SdkSourceServiceKeyExtractor` recipe exists for it, STOP and escalate — manifest MUST NOT get ahead of extractor. Add recipe + test first; then manifest entry.</trigger>
    <trigger>If `HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests` fails after DI 3-file edits, one of the three files is missing an update — diff all three against H4's exemplar and correct before proceeding.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: (a) H4 per-tenant handler (task 047, landed) — writes to per-tenant KV using literal or resolved values from `IKvSecretManifest`; NO source-extraction. (b) Manual ad-hoc bash extracted 6 F19 secrets SESSION 2 — no automation. (c) `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` (task 084, landed 2026-08-17 `70abd9992`) — has canonical names + `value_source` enum + never-delete flags, but NO source-extraction schema (`from-shared-service` value not in current allow-list). Grep for `ISourceServiceKeyExtractor` returns none across codebase.</existing>
    <extension>No — H4 per-tenant CANNOT be extended to also do source-extraction because (a) different KV scope (shared vs per-tenant), (b) different idempotency semantics (H4 rotation-safe by default; H4-shared verifies against fresh source every run and rotates on drift — CANNOT collapse these into one handler without conditional branches on every step), (c) different failure mode diagnostics (H4 write failure = permission/quota; H4-shared write failure = also permission/quota BUT ALSO source-service-unreachable + drift-detected + probe-verify-failure). Two sibling handlers keep each contract tight. Additively extending the shipped manifest (option A per Session 4 discussion) is the correct extension — the manifest schema was designed for this per task 084's `$AllowedValueSources` enum pattern.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H4-shared as a handler: (1) Every new Model 1 shared-tier deploy requires MANUAL ad-hoc bash to seed 6 secrets (SESSION 2 burned ~30 min; multiplied across N future customer stand-ups = N × 30 min waste). (2) Every source-service key rotation (Azure Portal → regenerate key1) silently breaks BFF startup until an operator manually re-seeds the KV — no drift detection today. (3) Model 2 Dedicated tier (per-customer, future) hits the SAME F19 pattern with per-customer source services; without H4-shared's source-extraction primitive, we would re-invent it for M2. Concrete observed failure mode SESSION 2: BFF exits with code 134 (SIGABRT) via `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException` for any of the 6 KV-referenced app settings not resolvable. F20 chain progressively reveals more.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

