  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a manifest with 6 shared-service entries + shared KV empty + L2 UAMI has Cognitive Services User / Search Service Contributor / Azure Service Bus Data Owner / Storage Account Contributor / Redis Cache Contributor on source services, when HandleAsync runs, then all 6 secrets are written to KV under canonical names via IKvSecretsWriter; each write is preceded by an ISourceServiceKeyExtractor call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-NO-OP: given the same manifest + KV state, second HandleAsync invocation performs 6 source-extractions (to verify) + 0 KV writes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-DRIFT-ROTATE: given a mocked source-drift for one entry, HandleAsync performs 1 rotation write + 0 writes for the other 5; audit log records rotation with entry name + old-value-hash + new-value-hash (never the values themselves).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BINDING guard: given a synthetic manifest that lists Dataverse-ClientSecret as `value_source: from-shared-service`, HandleAsync fails startup validation with "BindingPreCheckViolation" BEFORE any extractor or writer is called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-condition ref-resolution: after all writes, IArmKeyVaultRefProbe verifies each canonical secret name resolves via the App Service KV-ref binding; failure → HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "SharedSecretRefUnresolvable", diagnostic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Source-unreachable Quarantine: given mocked ISourceServiceKeyExtractor that throws RequestFailedException(status: 403), HandleAsync returns HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "SourceServiceExtractionFailed", diagnostic naming the failed service).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-key match: two invocations for the same (env, secretsVer) — second call short-circuits before source extraction (kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer} match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cleartext-secret leak scan: unit test greps Cosmos parameters + interStepState + all log statements for known secret patterns (test-manifest secret values); assert 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Manifest v1 backwards compat: entries in the manifest WITHOUT `value_source: from-shared-service` are skipped by H4-shared (they belong to H4 per-tenant flow); no error, no warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI via 3-file dance (HandlerIds const + keyed forwarder + concrete Worker registration); HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests passes.</criterion>
